            "license": "public domain",
            "source_url": "https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/The_Chinese_Classics/Volume_1/The_Great_Learning",
            "text": "Those of old who wished to make luminous virtue shine throughout the world first ordered their states; those who wished to order their states first regulated their families; those who wished to regulate their families first cultivated themselves; those who wished to cultivate themselves first rectified their hearts; those who wished to rectify their hearts first made their intentions sincere; those who wished to make their intentions sincere first extended their knowledge; extending knowledge lies in investigating things.",
            "translator": "Legge",
            "year": 1891
          }
